ct></svg><span class="stack-chip__name">Monte Carlo simulation</span></li></ul><p class="poster__links"><a class="mc-btn" href="/projects/st-petersburg">Full debrief →</a><a class="mc-btn" href="/docs/cs391-final-report.pdf">Paper ↗</a><a class="mc-btn" href="https://github.com/dannguyen111/saint-petersburg-AIDan-player" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code ↗</a></p></article><article class="poster" id="p-chomp" data-poster-panel="p-chomp" hidden aria-label="Poster: 3-Row Chomp: Making Byrnes Effective"><header class="poster__head"><div class="poster__id"><h3 class="poster__title">3-Row Chomp: Making Byrnes Effective</h3><p class="poster__sub">Aug 2025 – Present</p></div></header><div class="poster__cols"><div><h4 class="brief__label">Abstract</h4><p>Byrnes (2003) proved that in 3-row Chomp the losing positions of each row r eventually repeat with a fixed period, but his proof gives no bound on when the repetition starts. Can that preperiod N(r) be bounded explicitly?</p></div><div><h4 class="brief__label">Findings</h4><ul class="poster__list"><li>A streaming C++ solver computes exact losing positions for every row up to r = 50,000, validated against Brouwer&#39;s tables, Nivasch&#39;s census, OEIS, and a brute-force game tree.</li><li>Numerically, N(r) − √2·r stays within [−3.16, 5.70] for all r ≤ 50,000, sharpening the working conjecture to N(r) = √2·r + O(1).</li><li>The census turned up periods 6 and 8 beyond Nivasch&#39;s published set &#123;2, 3, 4, 9&#125;, first appearing at r = 11,036 and r = 18,718.</li><li>The two-pass referee gate has accepted an explicit computable bound, N(r) ≤ r + 2^O(r² log r), plus N(r) ≤ 3r for &quot;stale&quot; rows. Machine-refereed, not yet peer-reviewed.</li><li>From the 2025 capstone: proved by induction two infinite families of losing positions, (a+4, a+2, 2) and (a+11, a+7, 5), and conjectured the Gap Principle.</li></ul></div></div><div><h4 class="brief__label">Implications</h4><p>Next is a single human-checked write-up of the bound. Proving the &quot;locking&quot; lemma, which holds numerically up to r = 100,000, would give a linear bound N(r) ≤ 6r.</p></div><div><h4 class="brief__label">How it runs</h4><figure class="flow" aria-label="How 3-Row Chomp: Making Byrnes Effective runs, step by step"><figcaption class="flow__bar"><span class="flow__name">PIPELINE.EXE</span><span class="flow__lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></figcaption><ol class="flow__stages"><li class="flow__step"><div class="flow__stage"><span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div class="flow__text"><p class="flow__label">Solver</p><p class="flow__detail">Streaming C++ census of losing positions, cross-checked against the published literature.</p></div></div><span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span></li><li class="flow__step"><div class="flow__stage"><span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div class="flow__text"><p class="flow__label">Explorer</p><p class="flow__detail">MiMo-V2.6-Pro (xhigh reasoning) works one of two research islands, computing before it theorizes.</p></div></div><span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span></li><li class="flow__step"><div class="flow__stage"><span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div class="flow__text"><p class="flow__label">Ledger</p><p class="flow__detail">Every claim is logged with its evidence; failed ideas go to a dead-ends log.</p></div></div><span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span></li><li class="flow__step"><div class="flow__stage"><span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div class="flow__text"><p class="flow__label">Referee</p><p class="flow__detail">Two blind MiMo passes (temperature 0.3 and 0.8) see only the restated claim and a sandbox.</p></div></div><p class="flow__loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↺ </span>Split or reject → back to the explorer</p><span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span></li><li class="flow__step"><div class="flow__stage"><span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">05</span><div class="flow__text"><p class="flow__label">Proven</p><p class="flow__detail">Only an agreed, finished accept promotes a claim.</p></div></div><span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span></li><li class="flow__step"><div class="flow__stage"><span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">06</span><div class="flow__text"><p class="flow__label">Operator</p><p class="flow__detail">Claude Opus and I run novelty checks against prior art and read a daily digest.</p></div></div></li></ol></figure></div><h4 class="brief__label">Methods</h4><ul class="stack-chips"><li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #d9822b"><svg class="stack-chip__logo" viewBox="-1 -1 14 14" shape-rendering="crispEdges" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="-1" y="-1" width="14" height="14" fill="#f4efe2"></rect><rect x="1" y="0" width="10" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="0" y="1" width="12" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="0" y="2" width="12" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="0" y="3" width="3" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="3" y="3" width="2" height="1" fill="#fff"></rect><rect x="5" y="3" width="2" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="7" y="3" width="2" height="1" fill="#fff"></rect><rect x="9" y="3" width="3" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="0" y="4" width="2" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="2" y="4" width="1" height="1" fill="#fff"></rect><rect x="3" y="4" width="3" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="6" y="4" width="1" height="1" fill="#fff"></rect><rect x="7" y="4" width="5" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="0" y="5" width="2" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="2" y="5" width="1" height="1" fill="#fff"></rect><rect x="3" y="5" width="3" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="6" y="5" width="1" height="1" fill="#fff"></rect><rect x="7" y="5" width="1" height="1" fill="#d9822b"></rect><rect x="8" y="5" width="1" height="1" fill="#fff"></rect><rect x="9" y="5" width="3" he